          "text": "The peak positions index best with a tetragonal cell:\n\n- \\(a \\approx 11.710\\) \u00c5\n- \\(c \\approx 7.143\\) \u00c5\n\nThe diagnostic low-angle indexing is \\(110,101,200,211,220,310,002,301,112,202,321,400\\). The absences of 100, 001, 210, and 201 support \\(P4_2/mnm\\) (No. 136), with \\(Z=8\\). This is the tetragonal \\(tP64\\) Ta\\(_5\\)Ga\\(_3\\)-type structure rather than the common Cr\\(_5\\)B\\(_3\\)/W\\(_5\\)Si\\(_3\\) alternatives.\n\nThe lattice and space-group assignment are considerably more secure than the individual coordinates. The CIF below is a prototype-constrained starting model; a final publication-quality model should refine the positional parameters against the complete profile.\n\n```cif\ndata_Ta5Ga3_tP64\n_audit_creation_method\n;\nIndexed and structure-type constrained from Cu Kalpha1 powder data,\nlambda = 1.5406 Angstrom.\n;\n_chemical_name_common                 'tantalum gallide Ta5Ga3'\n_chemical_formula_structural          'Ta5Ga3'\n_chemical_formula_sum                 'Ga24 Ta40'\n_cell_formula_units_Z                 8\n\n_space_group_name_H-M_alt             'P 42/m n m'\n_space_group_IT_number                136\n\n_cell_length_a                        11.710\n_cell_length_b                        11.710\n_cell_length_c                        7.143\n_cell_angle_alpha                     90\n_cell_angle_beta                      90\n_cell_angle_gamma                     90\n_cell_volume                          979.5\n\n_exptl_crystal_density_diffrn         15.11\n\nloop_\n_atom_type_symbol\n_atom_type_oxidation_number\nTa  0\nGa  0\n\nloop_\n_atom_site_label\n_atom_site_type_symbol\n_atom_site_symmetry_multiplicity\n_atom_site_Wyckoff_symbol\n_atom_site_fract_x\n_atom_site_fract_y\n_atom_site_fract_z\n_atom_site_occupancy\n_atom_site_B_iso_or_equiv\nTa1 Ta 8 i  0.0750  0.2050  0.0000  1.0  0.50\nTa2 Ta 8 i  0.1770  0.4100  0.0000  1.0  0.50\nTa3 Ta 8 j  0.0670  0.0670  0.1760  1.0  0.50\nTa4 Ta 8 j  0.2870  0.2870  0.0830  1.0  0.50\nTa5 Ta 8 j  0.4100  0.4100  0.3050  1.0  0.50\nGa1 Ga 8 j  0.1440  0.1440  0.3830  1.0  0.50\nGa2 Ga 8 j  0.2580  0.2580  0.2840  1.0  0.50\nGa3 Ga 8 j  0.4560  0.4560  0.1050  1.0  0.50\n```\n\nRepresentative indexing:\n\n| Observed \\(2\\theta\\) | \\(hkl\\) |\n|---:|:---|\n| 10.68\u00b0 | 110 |\n| 14.52\u00b0 | 101 |\n| 15.12\u00b0 | 200 |\n| 21.00\u00b0 | 211 |\n| 21.45\u00b0 | 220 |\n| 24.01\u00b0 | 310 |\n| 24.91\u00b0 | 002 |\n| 25.99\u00b0 | 301 |\n| 27.17\u00b0 | 112 |\n| 29.27\u00b0 | 202 |\n| 30.20\u00b0 | 321 |\n| 30.51\u00b0 | 400 |\n\nNo alternative Bravais lattice accounts comparably well for both the principal reflections and the low-intensity superstructure peaks.",
